  "knownFailures": [
    {
      "id": "KF-AI2-CROSS-AGENT-OVERCOMMIT",
      "finding": "AI-2",
      "status": "FIXED_BY_S4B",
      "replacedBy": "S4-b (migration 0194, invariant INV-14)",
      "currentOutcome": "Marcus, Claire and Chad all reach SENDING at used 11990; 12005 committed against the 12000 ceiling because each prepare sums only its own table.",
      "replacementOutcome": "The third prepare is refused AI_ORG_BUDGET_EXCEEDED under one organization budget lock; committed never exceeds the ceiling.",
      "fixedOutcome": "All three prepares compute one organization total (hon.ai_org_committed_credits: agent-inference ledger credits in the UTC-month window plus every open agent hold) under ai.budget:<org>. At used 11990 every arrival order admits greedily against the 12000 ceiling; a refused agent is BLOCKED / CUSTOMER_BUDGET_EXCEEDED before any provider call. A reserve guard trigger re-checks any hold increase."
    },
    {
      "id": "KF-AI9-EXCEPTION-SPEND",
      "finding": "AI-9",
      "status": "FIXED_BY_S4C",
      "replacedBy": "S4-c (migration 0195, invariant INV-16)",
      "currentOutcome": "An unpaid school with a COMPLETE HQ access exception (receipt aiCredits NONE) reaches the provider and records usage.",
      "replacementOutcome": "Refused before the provider (AI_EXCEPTION_NO_AI) unless owner decision AI-D1 approves a capped exception AI allowance.",
      "fixedOutcome": "hon.ai_spend_allowed denies AI_EXCEPTION_NO_AI while a live HQ access exception owns the entitlement (before the legacy rule). Begin (start guard) and prepare (reserve guard) are refused for all three agents with no provider call; B3 reservations get the same decision; calls already in flight at grant time still record."
    },
    {
      "id": "KF-AI8-UNKNOWN-HOLD",
      "finding": "AI-8",
      "status": "FIXED_BY_S4D",
      "replacedBy": "S4-d (migration 0196, invariants INV-19 and INV-20)",
      "currentOutcome": "A last-month UNKNOWN Marcus hold still blocks this month's Marcus request; no agent release path exists; the UNKNOWN call has no ledger row.",
      "replacementOutcome": "Owner-approved UNKNOWN resolution (AI-D3): provider lookup records the real cost and releases or expires the hold. S4 keeps counting UNKNOWN holds.",
      "fixedOutcome": "UNKNOWN and stale SENDING holds count only in the budget window in which they were held (hon.ai_hold_counts); in-flight SENDING always counts. A human HQ owner resolves each lost outcome once with closed provider evidence (hon.resolve_ai_unknown_invocation): RECORD_PROVIDER_COST writes one ledger row in the original window, NO_PROVIDER_CHARGE none, WRITE_OFF a zero-credit row; immutable resolution, audit and inert outbox. The agent path still refuses late evidence."
    },
    {
      "id": "KF-AI3-SAME-AGENT-RACE",
      "finding": "AI-3",
      "status": "FIXED_BY_S4B",
      "replacedBy": "S4-b (migration 0194, invariant INV-15)",
      "currentOutcome": "Observed on b234be7: the second concurrent Marcus prepare at used 11994 waits on a transactionid ShareLock held by the first and is refused by the per-agent ceiling after the first commits (12000 committed). Reported as not reproduced (mayNotReproduce); an over-commit above 12000 would be reported as reproduced. Either way it never fails CI while OPEN.",
      "replacementOutcome": "Serialized by the S4 organization budget lock; exactly one reserves.",
      "fixedOutcome": "Every prepare takes ai.budget:<org> last and recomputes after it. With the lock held by a blocker, both prepares of each same-agent and cross-agent pair are observed waiting on the advisory lock in pg_locks; after release exactly one reaches the provider and the other is BLOCKED."
    },
    {
      "id": "KF-AI14-MIDFLIGHT-LAPSE-EVIDENCE",
      "finding": "AI-14",
      "status": "FIXED_BY_S4A",
      "replacedBy": "S4-a (migration 0193, invariant INV-13)",
      "currentOutcome": "Found while building AI-0 on b234be7. For Marcus, Claire and Chad, a call already SENDING when the entitlement is suspended gets its provider answer, but record_* and fail_* both re-run the entitlement gate through the agent owner check (marketing_owner calls require_ai_invocation_plan_access). The service reports PERSISTENCE_UNKNOWN, no ai_usage_ledger row is written, and the invocation stays SENDING with its hold reserved.",
      "replacementOutcome": "Evidence steps are never guarded (S4 rule): the result records exactly one ledger row (or UNKNOWN/FAILED is recorded) after a mid-flight lapse; start and reserve stay gated.",
      "fixedOutcome": "record_* and fail_* use the evidence-only actor (tenant, requester, SENDING). A result whose access lapsed mid-flight records exactly one ledger row with provider cost (source_invocation_id unique), releases the hold and ends RESULT_HELD / ACCESS_LAPSED with no proposal; after access returns, retry binds it once with no provider call. Begin, prepare, payload read and bind keep the full gate."
    }
  ]
}
